#
# File: 250-ARP-Flux-reply-in-monitor.rule
# Policy: Monitor incoming replies claiming the local interface IPv4 address from its expected MAC
# Description:
#     Runs after ARP hook and zone interface map/vmap dispatch; no interface matching here.
#     This is only a diagnostic indicator; ARP flux is an interface/ownership behavior.
#     Mismatched MAC claims are handled by the duplicate-address guard.
#     Direction: remote-to-local; intended for arp input hook.
#
arp operation reply arp saddr ip $ZONE_INTF_IPADDR arp saddr ether $ZONE_INTF_MACADDR counter comment "remote-to-local Local address reply monitor"
